# Example environment file.
#
# Copy it to .env:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# DEVELOPMENT
# -----------
# When OAUTH_ENV is dev/development/local/test, the server generates ephemeral
# values for OAUTH_KEY_ENCRYPTION_KEY and OAUTH_AUDIT_PEPPER when they are unset,
# so a fresh checkout boots with no setup. Generated secrets are per-process:
# encrypted rows (TOTP secrets, client secrets) do NOT survive a restart. That is
# fine for development and unacceptable anywhere else.
#
# PRODUCTION
# ----------
# Both secrets MUST be set. Each is 32 bytes given as 64 hex characters:
#     openssl rand -hex 32
# The loader refuses to start if either is missing, is still an example value, or
# decodes to the wrong length.
#
#   OAUTH_KEY_ENCRYPTION_KEY  must decode to exactly 32 bytes
#   OAUTH_AUDIT_PEPPER        must decode to at least 32 bytes
#
# Everything else lives in config.yaml. docker-compose.yml supplies the service
# hostnames (postgres, redis, mailhog) through OAUTH_-prefixed variables. Any
# setting can be overridden the same way, for example:
#
#   OAUTH_SERVER_ISSUER=https://sso.example.com
#   OAUTH_DATABASE_URL=postgres://oauth:oauth@postgres:5432/oauth?sslmode=disable
#   OAUTH_REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379/0
#
# Leave these unset in development to use generated values:
# OAUTH_KEY_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
# OAUTH_AUDIT_PEPPER=
